# Context

## Background
The libc crate exposes setrlimit resource arguments with platform-specific public types. The glibc-private __rlimit_resource_t alias is absent on macOS and musl.

## Why This Way
A local macro lets each RLIMIT_* constant flow directly into the platform setrlimit signature, avoiding a guessed cross-platform alias while keeping the same limits. Integration fixtures now seed disclosure revision 2 so a clean CI build does not emit the expected first-use notice into unrelated stream assertions.

## Gotchas
Use a clean Cargo target when verifying integration binaries locally: cargo package/install jobs can overwrite target/debug/uhm with a packaged-source build while Cargo fingerprints remain fresh.
